Applying matrix product rules yields:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\gamma\boldsymbol{X} & =\left(\boldsymbol{I}-\frac{1}{N}\boldsymbol{11}^{\top}\right)\boldsymbol{X}\\
 & =\boldsymbol{X}-\frac{1}{N}\boldsymbol{11}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}\\
 & =\boldsymbol{X}-\boldsymbol{1}\frac{1}{N}\boldsymbol{1}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}\\
 & =\boldsymbol{X}-\boldsymbol{1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\boldsymbol{X}^{\top}\boldsymbol{1}\right)^{\top}\\
 & =\boldsymbol{X}-\boldsymbol{1}\bar{\boldsymbol{x}}^{\top}\\
 & =\boldsymbol{Z}
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The last equality is seen by looking at an arbitrary row 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

