\begin_layout Standard
For every column 
\begin_inset Formula $c$
\end_inset

 in 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{Z}$
\end_inset

 the last coordinate (or any one coordinate i just choose the last for notational convenience) equals the negative sum over the 
\begin_inset Formula $N-1$
\end_inset

 other elements of the column 
\begin_inset Formula $c$
\end_inset

:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\sum^{N-1}_{n=1}z_{nc} & =x_{1c}-\frac{1}{N}\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}+x_{2c}-\frac{1}{N}\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}+\cdots+x_{(N-1)c}-\frac{1}{N}\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}\\
 & =\sum^{N-1}_{n=1}x_{nc}-\frac{1}{N}\left((N-1)\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}\right)\\
 & =\sum^{N-1}_{n=1}x_{nc}-\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}+\frac{1}{N}\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}\\
 & =-\left(x_{Nc}-\frac{1}{N}\sum^{N}_{n=1}x_{nc}\right)\\
 & =-z_{Nc}.
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus the whole last row is a linear function of the 
\begin_inset Formula $N-1$
\end_inset

 rows 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\boldsymbol{z}^{\top}_{N}=-\sum^{N-1}_{n=1}\boldsymbol{z}^{\top}_{n},
\]

